CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-narrow-shared
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
The same program as narrow_shared_mutex with the narrowing turned off. The two
encodings have to agree; this is the arm that says so.

--no-narrow-shared reproduces the pre-narrowing formula to the digit on the
benchmarks it was measured on (28-race_reach_81-list_racing: 184325 variables,
695392 clauses either way), so it is also the control for showing that the
change is confined to the narrowed path.
